                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "(Received for free via developer's key submission for SteadyGiveaways.  Thanks, man!)\n\n[h1]Vlad's the name, [i]Impale[/i]'s my game![/h1]\n\n...Okay, well...maybe not...  [i]Impale[/i] is a simple physics-based puzzle game similar to that of [i]Save Jesus[/i] and [i]Zombie Ballz[/i] (which I'm credited in) with 50 levels ranging from easy to skill-based solutions to luck-based solutions.\n\nBasically, there are some puzzles I liked and others I didn't like so much.  Though there were plenty of ways to kill the zombies, and all methods must be done to pass a level.  Really ended fp hating the levels that were completely luck-based, but it's not a bad game...just in need of balancing for the casual gamer.\n\nIt's a little hard to rate this game, but if I had to say whether or not to try it, I'd say it's worth your time, but not full price ($2).  Wait for it to go on sale for $1 for it to feel more worth your money, though it may feel like less than that.  Don't purchase if you're impatient.\n\n5/10  It's not bad, but I've seen worse games out there.",
